<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<title>Sign Up</title>
<link rel="stylesheet" href="/sign-up-style.css">
<script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/sweetalert2@11"></script>
<style>
    body {
        font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;
        background-image: url(/sign-up-bg.svg);
        margin: 0;
        padding: 0;
        overflow: hidden;
    }

</style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="container">
    <div class="form-container">
        <form id="signupForm">
            <label for="studentName">Student's Name:</label>
            <input type="text" name="studentName" id="studentName" required><br>
            <label for="schoolId">School ID:</label>
            <input type="text" name="schoolId" id="schoolId" required><br>
            <label for="email">Email Address:</label>
            <input type="email" name="email" id="email" required><br>
            <label for="password">Password:</label>
            <input type="password" name="password" id="password" required><br>
            <input type="submit" value="Sign Up">
        </form>
    </div>
    <div class="scrollable-container">
        <h2>Privacy Policy</h2>
            <p>● Information Collection: We collect personal information for children under 13 with parental
            consent, ensuring compliance with Philippine data privacy laws and safeguarding the
            privacy of young users.</p>
            <p>● Usage of Information: Personal information is solely used to provide services and customize
            the user experience for children aged 1-7. Non-personal information is utilized for analytics
            purposes to enhance our services.</p>
            <p>● Sharing of Information: We do not sell personal information and share it only as mandated
            by Philippine data privacy laws or to provide services. Non-personal information may be
            shared with third-party service providers for analytics, adhering to data privacy regulations.</p>
            <p>● Data Security: While we employ industry-standard security measures to protect personal
            information, we acknowledge the limitations inherent in online platforms and strive to
            maintain robust data security practices.</p>
            <p>● Children's Privacy: We strictly adhere to the Philippine Data Privacy Act and obtain parental
            consent before collecting personal information from children under 13, ensuring
            compliance with local regulations and fostering a safe online environment for young users.</p>
            <p>● Changes to Privacy Policy: Significant changes to our privacy policy will be communicated to
            parents or guardians in compliance with Philippine data privacy laws, promoting
            transparency and user awarenes</p>
        <h2>Terms of Use</h2>
            <p>● Use of Services: Children aged 1-7 may use KidVerse with parental consent, ensuring
            compliance with Philippine data privacy regulations and fostering a safe online
            environment.</p>
            <p>● User Content: Children are expected to upload appropriate content in adherence to
            Philippine laws and regulations, promoting positive interactions and respectful behavior.</p>
            <p>● Intellectual Property: Children must respect copyright laws and refrain from unauthorized
            use of KidVerse content, in accordance with Philippine intellectual property regulations.</p>
            <p>● Limitation of Liability: KidVerse provides services "as is" and is not liable for damages
            arising from use, adhering to Philippine legal standards regarding liability limitations.</p>
            <p>● Governing Law: These terms are governed by Philippine laws, with any disputes resolved in
            Philippine courts, ensuring legal clarity and jurisdictional compliance.
            Parents or guardians allowing their children to use KidVerse agree to adhere to these summarized
            terms and policies, promoting the safe, secure, and compliant use of the platform for young users
            aged 1-7 in the Philippines</p>
        <input type="checkbox" id="agreeCheckbox">
        <label for="agreeCheckbox">I agree to the terms and conditions</label>
    </div>
</div>

<button class="back-button" onclick="window.location.href='/';">
    <img src="/back-arrow-icon.png" alt="Back">
</button>

<script>
    document.getElementById('signupForm').addEventListener('submit', async function(event) {
        event.preventDefault();
        const formData = new FormData(this);
        if (!document.getElementById('agreeCheckbox').checked) {
            Swal.fire('Please agree to the terms and conditions');
            return; 
        }
        try {
            const response = await fetch('/signup', {
                method: 'POST',
                body: new URLSearchParams(formData)
            });

            const responseData = await response.json();

            if (response.ok) {
                Swal.fire({
                    title: 'Success!',
                    text: responseData.message,
                    icon: 'success'
                }).then(() => {
                    window.location.href = '/';
                });
            } else {
                Swal.fire({
                    title: 'Error!',
                    text: responseData.error,
                    icon: 'error'
                });
            }
        } catch (error) {
            console.error('Error:', error);
            Swal.fire({
                title: 'Error!',
                text: 'An error occurred. Please try again later.',
                icon: 'error'
            });
        }
    });
</script>
</body>
</html>
